# Raw import archives (checklistbank DwCAs, GBIF NameUsage dumps, etc.).
# These are downloaded inputs, not source — keep them out of the repo.
# q-bert keeps the same archives under /home/agent/sources/archives/.
archives/
node_modules/
shared/node_modules
dist/
.DS_Store
*.local
.env
# Screenshots / dev captures — keep in tmp/, never commit
*.png
tmp/
portal/data/unified-taxonomy.json
portal/data/unified-taxonomy-skeleton.json
portal/data/order-manifest.json
portal/data/coverage-summary.json
portal/data/orders/
portal/test-results/
.playwright-mcp/
portal/data/gbif-cache-*.json
portal/data/gbif-cache-*.json.gz
portal/data/gbif-cache-*.zip
portal/data/wcvp-cache*.json
portal/data/gbif-keys-*.json
portal/data/powo-ipni-cache*.json
portal/data/powo-fields-cache*.json
.opencode/
*.log
*.tmp
*.bat
# Nothing under scripts/ is ignored on purpose. There used to be rules here for
# fix_*.py, enrich_*.py, gen_*.py, add_*.py and expand_*.py, but every file
# they matched is already tracked - 7 fixers, 18 enrich passes, and one each of
# gen/add/expand - so the rules could not affect any of them and only hid new
# ones. Adding scripts/fix_redirect_descriptions.py silently produced nothing
# and needed `git add -f`, which is the worst way for a rule to behave. Kept
# here so nobody adds them back: if a script is worth writing it is worth
# committing, and one-shot scratch work belongs in /tmp, not the repo.
*.bak
__pycache__/
.Rhistory
# Derived data indexes, re-fetchable and far too large for git. Each has a
# builder script; see the docstring for the source URL.
#   mycobank-index.json      200 MB, from mycobank.org/Images/MBList.zip
#                           (scripts/buildMycobankIndex.py)
#   name-parse-shards/       ~99 MB per 3 shards, the GBIF parser output,
#                           merged into name-parse-index.jsonl by
#                           scripts/parseAllNamesSliced.sh
portal/data/mycobank-index.json
portal/data/gbif-continents-index.json
portal/data/gbif-vernacular-index.json
portal/data/itis-vernacular-index.json
portal/data/gbif-locality-index.json
portal/data/name-parse-shards/
portal/data/name-parse-index.jsonl
# pending-family worklist: a symlink to the external store, not repo data
portal/data/pending-families.jsonl
# unresolved-kingdom-taxa worklist: same treatment, same reasoning
portal/data/pending-unresolved-taxa.jsonl
# dedupe-log.jsonl: same treatment -- an append-only machine log that hit
# GitHub's 100MB hard limit on 2026-10-22 (112MB, 278k lines, 5 days of
# dedupeSpeciesAcrossFamilies.py runs); moved to the external volume with
# a symlink in its place, same as pending-families.jsonl above
data/dedupe-log.jsonl
portal/data/inat-common-names.jsonl
data/.maintenance.lock
portal/data/unified-taxonomy-plantae.json
portal/data/unified-taxonomy-skeleton-plantae.json
portal/data/order-manifest-plantae.json
portal/data/coverage-summary-plantae.json
portal/data/orders-plantae/
portal/data/kingdoms/

# Derived flat projection of the tree, for ad-hoc DuckDB queries. Rebuilt from
# the family files by scripts/buildSpeciesParquet.py; never read by the app.
# 47 MB for 2.35M species, ~82s to build.
portal/data/species.parquet
portal/data/species.parquet.jsonl
portal/data/.species-cache-*.parquet
portal/data/.species-cache-*.parquet.jsonl
portal/data/species-count-cache.json

# Per-family name-parse-index sidecars — derived from name-parse-index.jsonl
# by scripts/splitNameIndex.py; regenerated per machine for incremental sync.
portal/data/name-parse-index/

# (kingdom, authority, key) -> species, for the import-time duplicate gate.
# Rebuilt from the family files by scripts/authorityIndex.py (and lazily,
# automatically, by merge_family itself whenever it is older than the newest
# family file); never read by the app.
portal/data/.authority-index.sqlite3
# scripts/genusAuthorityRegister.py's aggregated genus-level nomenclatural
# register (IRMNG + Nomenclator Zoologicus + Species Fungorum Plus); derived
# from archives on the sources volume, rebuilt automatically when stale.
portal/data/.genus-authority-register.sqlite3
portal/public/data/kingdoms/
portal/public/data/book/
portal/data/non-english-descriptions.jsonl
portal/data/commons-credits.jsonl
portal/data/inat-fetch-state.json

# Runtime import/build action log. Append-only JSONL written by
# portal/scripts/lib/importActions.ts (TS builds) and scripts/import_actions.py
# (Python imports) — one line per start/finish/error/interrupted/uuid-stamp
# event, so a killed run leaves a reconstructable record of what it did.
# Grows unbounded and is regenerated on every run; never version it.
portal/data/import-actions.jsonl

# Stripped from history 2026-10-10 (exceeded GitHub's 100MB hard limit and
# were blocking every push since). Both regenerable/downloaded, never meant
# to be versioned: sanity-queue.json is a scan snapshot
# (python3 scripts/sanity_scan.py taxonomy --write), MBList.xlsx is the raw
# MycoBank download (mycobank.org/Images/MBList.zip) that builds the
# already-gitignored mycobank-index.json.
portal/data/sanity-queue.json
portal/data/MBList.xlsx
~$*
sanity-issues.json
portal/data/sanity-issues.json
